9. REDUCE ALL EXISTING PRICES BY 20%
==================================================

Apply a one-time reduction of 20% to every current numeric service
price and every current numeric package price across all six
markets:

- Tunisia.
- Algeria.
- Libya.
- Europe.
- Canada.
- International.

This includes all numeric prices currently stored in:
- INITIAL_DEPARTMENTS.
- INITIAL_PACKAGES.
- Any existing persisted pricing records used by the application.

Reduce every currently configured numeric amount and both ends
of each configured price range by 20%.

Keep the same currency, market assignment, billing interval,
pricing type, service ID and package ID.

ROUNDING:

Tunisia (TND):
Round to practical amounts, generally the nearest 10 TND.

Algeria (DZD):
Round to practical amounts, generally the nearest 500 DZD
or another sensible local increment for the price magnitude.

Libya (LYD):
Round to practical amounts, generally the nearest 10 LYD.

Europe (EUR):
Round to the nearest €5 or €10 as appropriate.

Canada (CAD):
Round to the nearest C$5 or C$10 as appropriate.

International (USD):
Round to the nearest $5 or $10 as appropriate.

Do not change one market's price by converting another market's
price through exchange rates.

Do not change non-numeric "Custom quote" or "Not yet published"
records into numeric prices.

Apply the reduction exactly once.

IMPORTANT PERSISTENCE RULE:

Inspect src/lib/storage.ts and the existing persistence mechanism.

If previously saved prices override INITIAL_DEPARTMENTS or
INITIAL_PACKAGES, implement a one-time price migration with a
version marker.

Apply the 20% reduction exactly once to the current stored price
records, including previously persisted prices, while preserving
their current market and billing assignments.

Record that the migration has been applied.

Do not reduce prices again on every page load or every restart.

Do not overwrite future administrator edits by repeating the
migration.

Do not reduce a second time if the migration marker is already
present.

The result must be consistent in the public website, selection
drawer, package cards, pricing matrix, promotion calculations,
and admin preview.

